 motions  were running very high as the  jurors read out their verdicts first of  all kyle rittenhouse the defendant broke  down essentially shaking all over his  body was then escorted out of the  courtroom very quickly after that and in  contrast the family members of the  victims  crying sobbing as they left the  courtroom  outside here some people honking their  horns celebrating others frustrated  arguing debating i can't believe that  this has really happened and of course  we shouldn't forget michael that this is  not only about the town of kenosha this  is a co this is a trial that was  followed very closely all across the  united states that divides the nation  and so a lot of people will be either  relieved or very frustrated with today's  today's verdict oliver as you well know  we cannot overstate how highly  anticipated this verdict was is there  concern at this hour about how  communities are going to react to this  verdict particularly those communities  that were involved in these racial  justice protests in the first place  now of course there are concerns  especially here in kenosha because let's  remind our viewers when this happened  here when kyle rittenhouse  shot at those three of those three  people here those were blm protesters  that night taking to the street in  support of jacob blake  that black man that was shot by a white  police officer so a lot of people here  will be frustrated the question is will  they come will they come out will they  protest tonight we can hear some  helicopters in the sky but overall the  situation here at least in kenosha on  the ground has been very quiet as of now  and let's not forget again that there's  a bigger question you know behind all  this a lot of people and critics are  concerned that this is a blueprint now  for people  essentially saying that this ruling  means it's okay to take your gun your  assault rifle on a protest and then act  in self-defense later and a lot of other  questions that follow is this a question  of white privilege for instance that  verdict that we had here today questions  of gun laws will be asked that are  dividing the nation as well and perhaps  the most important question what would  have happened um if kyle rittenhouse was  a black citizen would we have seen  another verdict then  oliver uh before this verdict came in of  course there was a request from the  defense for a mistrial  on what basis did they ask for the judge  to throw this case out  yeah there were several of those  requests but perhaps the most important  one was the one that we heard  just in the final days here  it was about drone footage that was shot  about the drone footage of the last  shots that he fired on mr rosenbaum the  first victim  and the  defendants say that that footage was not  handed over to them in full resolution  whereas the prosecution had full  resolution so they saw some kind of a  disadvantage over there look  since there is a verdict now and the  verdict is not guilty all those bids  are not relevant anymore because kyle  rittenhouse is now unguilty on all  counts that's right uh oliver salad in  kenosha many thanks oliver
 

